reg: cs-technical-writing; canon: runbook composition over a closed-world CLI artifact (bash/systemd vocabulary, rsync mirror semantics, citation register A9/A12/A13/A14/A18/A23).
defs:
  I1 := tool = runs/001-hermes-context-timer/artifact/sync-hermes-context.sh (+ service, timer, README)
  I2 := env: HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC, HERMES_CONTEXT_DST override defaults /opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/ -> /workspace/hermes-context/
  I3 := flags closed world: --dry-run (plan, zero writes), --verify (exit 0 iff exact mirror, nonzero+A9 else), real run = one-way recursive mirror, removes stale DST extras, preserves types+symlink targets, re-verifies; any other flag = usage error exit 2
  I4 := install targets: ~/.local/bin (script), ~/.config/systemd/user/ (units); timer period = 6h; real runs log one line to ~/.cache/hermes-context/
  I5 := citation register: A23 set-but-empty env (unset falls back to prod defaults); A18 degenerate paths (empty/'.',->/); A12 same/ancestor/descendant/symlink-component; A13 staging verification failed (DST untouched); A14 staging conflicts incl. TMPDIR set-but-empty (TMPDIR may set staging parent); A9 mirror-mismatch findings; other refusals -> describe condition, no citation
  I6 := deliverable = single RUNBOOK.md, sections in fixed order: What this tool does; Test before installing (--dry-run); Install; Configure (change the source); Schedule (systemd user timer); Verify a sync; Roll back a bad sync; Troubleshooting (A-number meanings)
  I7 := rollback = remove bad HERMES_CONTEXT_DST then re-sync from known-good SRC (configured HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC); disabling timer alone = insufficient
invariants:
  A9_closedworld: ∀ claim in RUNBOOK.md -> claim ∈ facts(I1..I7) ∨ artifact-verifiable; else DELETE claim
  A7_exec: ∀ instruction block -> executable verbatim from arbitrary cwd (emit literal `cd /workspace/hdcs/runs/001-hermes-context-timer/artifact` or absolute paths); marked `# example:` config lines exempt
  A5_asdelivered: document refusals as delivered, not idealized
  A3_register: hcdl register terms (A-number, packet, seat) explained or omitted in runbook body
  A1_mk1: RUNBOOK documents HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC + HERMES_CONTEXT_DST exactly (verbatim)
  A1_mk2: RUNBOOK includes pre-install --dry-run test (runnable)
  A1_mk3: RUNBOOK states concrete rollback action
  mkdir_rule: install section teaches mkdir -p / install -D; no assumption dirs exist
  scope_note: --checksum/--delete/--itemize-changes are rsync internal flags, never taught as tool flags
open: none — all operator rulings recorded; packet READY for scoped-build (S2 drafts RUNBOOK.md against rubric A7).
